The IFC web experience has two viewer implementations. The xeokit path loads
server-generated XKT through `@xeokit/xeokit-sdk`. The web-ifc path reads IFC
directly in the browser through web-ifc and Three.js, without using XKT at
runtime. The server-side converter separately uses `@xeokit/xeokit-convert`
and web-ifc to generate XKT and metadata.

The tracked `web/public/wasm/web-ifc*.wasm` files are web-ifc distribution
artifacts and remain subject to MPL-2.0. Although the two viewer paths are
separate implementations, the current standard web build includes both and
declares xeokit as a dependency. Selecting web-ifc at runtime does not remove
xeokit from the distributed build. Deployments and redistributed builds must
therefore be reviewed against the licenses of the components actually included
in the build. A xeokit-free deployment requires a separately verified build
that does not include or depend on xeokit. Dependency manifests and lockfiles
contain exact versions.

